      "git_blob_sha": "908bec7fa75b5915128fa07f664342100b34ddbe",
      "stable_id": "R-HSA-9007926",
      "display_name": "ATRX binds DAXX",
      "species": "Homo sapiens",
      "summary": "ATRX (Alpha-thalassemia mental retardation syndrome X-linked) binds to transcriptional co-activator DAXX (Death domain-associated protein 6) to form an ATP-dependent chromatin remodeling complex with triple-helix displacement activity (Xue et al. 2003)."
    },
    {
      "canonical_path": "reactome/R-HSA-9670101.md",
      "archive_member": "gene_candidates/ATRX/reactome/R-HSA-9670101.md",
      "staged_path": "tmp/seed34-verified-staging/quarantine/auxiliary/gene_candidates/ATRX/reactome/R-HSA-9670101.md",
      "kind": "reactome",
      "bytes": 1016,
      "sha256": "e33e82e7ba1230070020eb7b2463696cf33a74ab455240dc01539dcaf8a2ad88",
      "git_blob_sha": "32228469f75741c4105cdcd0d5ba13423f7e5c55",
      "stable_id": "R-HSA-9670101",
      "display_name": "ATRX:DAXX binds to subtelomeric chromosomal regions",
      "species": "Homo sapiens",
      "summary": "The complex of ATRX (Alpha-thalassemia mental retardation syndrome X-linked) and DAXX (Death domain-associated protein 6) binds to subtelomeric chromosomal regions and plays a role in the recruitment of cohesin to subtelomeric regions and in the regulation of transcription of the noncoding telomeric repeat-containing RNA (TERRA) (Eid et al. 2015)."
    },
    {
      "canonical_path": "reactome/R-HSA-9670114.md",
      "archive_member": "gene_candidates/ATRX/reactome/R-HSA-9670114.md",
      "staged_path": "tmp/seed34-verified-staging/quarantine/auxiliary/gene_candidates/ATRX/reactome/R-HSA-9670114.md",
      "kind": "reactome",
      "bytes": 1202,
      "sha256": "fc9b3c18bb7a0cdfe666d6214e66c54c87d6272d69de884f4b9e7aace80a51b2",
      "git_blob_sha": "d1043cd629ad5e22ebb7b9c0c83cf15e1d81ffce",
      "stable_id": "R-HSA-9670114",
      "display_name": "Histone H3.3 deposition at telomere",
      "species": "Homo sapiens",
      "summary": "ATRX (Alpha-thalassemia mental retardation syndrome X-linked) and its binding partner DAXX (Death domain-associated protein 6) are required for deposition of histone H3.3, encoded by either the H3F3A gene or the H3F3B gene, to telomeres, independently of the H3.3 chaperone HIRA, in both human and mouse embryonic stem cells. Highly evolutionarily conserved N-terminus of DAXX interacts directly with the H3.3 core (Goldberg et al. 2010, Lewis et al. 2010)."
    },
    {
